const Q_R2_ABERTAS_TRANSPORTE = [
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F65b", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 5 — Checksums.</b> Um datagrama UDP tem estes 16 bytes (linhas de 32 bits):<br><code>01001010 01101010 11011011 00101000</code><br><code>00000000 00010000 00000000 00000000</code><br><code>10100010 10101010 10000001 11110101</code><br><code>11010001 11101000 10001010 10110111</code><br><br>(a) Quais são as portas e o tamanho do datagrama? (b) Calcula o checksum, põe-no no datagrama e verifica-o.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>(a)</strong> Palavras de 16 bits, por ordem: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_1</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0100101001101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_2</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101101100101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_3</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000010000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_4</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000000000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_5</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1010001010101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_6</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000000111110101</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_7</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101000111101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_8</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000101010110111</code>.</p>\n<p>O cabeçalho UDP tem 4 campos de 16 bits, por esta ordem: porta de origem, porta de destino, comprimento e <em>checksum</em>. Em <em>network order</em> (<em>big endian</em>), o primeiro byte é o mais significativo:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>porta de origem <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= w_1</annotation></semantics></math> = <code>0100101001101010</code> $= 2<sup>{14}+2</sup>{11}+2<sup>{9}+2</sup>{6}+2<sup>{5}+2</sup>{3}+2^{1} = 16384+2048+512+64+32+8+2 = $ <strong>19050</strong>;</li>\n<li>porta de destino <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= w_2</annotation></semantics></math> = <code>1101101100101000</code> $= 32768+16384+4096+2048+512+256+32+8 = $ <strong>56104</strong>;</li>\n<li>comprimento <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= w_3</annotation></semantics></math> = <code>0000000000010000</code> $= $ <strong>16 bytes</strong> (8 de cabeçalho + 8 de dados: as duas últimas linhas);</li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_4</annotation></semantics></math> = 0: o campo do <em>checksum</em> ainda não foi preenchido.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> Palavras de 16 bits, por ordem: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_1</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0100101001101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_2</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101101100101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_3</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000010000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_4</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000000000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_5</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1010001010101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_6</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000000111110101</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_7</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101000111101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_8</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000101010110111</code>.</p>\n<p>Soma com <em>wraparound</em> (quando passa de 16 bits, o 1 da esquerda soma-se à direita), com o campo do <em>checksum</em> a zeros:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">passo</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">soma</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">resultado (16 bits)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_1</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0100101001101010</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_2</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>1 0010010110010010</code> → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0010010110010011</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_3</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">sem transporte</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0010010110100011</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_4</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">(zeros)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0010010110100011</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_5</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">sem transporte</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>1100100001001101</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_6</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>1 0100101001000010</code> → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0100101001000011</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_7</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>1 0001110000101011</code> → <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>0001110000101100</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">+\\,w_8</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">sem transporte</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><code>1010011011100011</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Soma = <code>1010011011100011</code>; <strong><em>checksum</em></strong> = complemento para 1 = <strong><code>0101100100011100</code></strong> (0x591C). O datagrama fica com a 2.ª linha <code>00000000 00010000 01011001 00011100</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Verificação</strong> (receptor: soma tudo, com o <em>checksum</em>): <code>1010011011100011 + 0101100100011100 = 1111111111111111</code>. Tudo uns: nenhum erro detetado.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> soma com wraparound, depois complemento para 1; o receptor tem de obter tudo uns.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#udp-e-o-checksum\" target=\"_blank\">📖 UDP e o checksum</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F65d", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 5 — Checksums.</b> Um datagrama UDP tem estes 16 bytes (linhas de 32 bits):<br><code>01001010 01101010 11011011 00101000</code><br><code>00000000 00010000 00000000 00000000</code><br><code>10100010 10101010 10000001 11110101</code><br><code>11010001 11101000 10001010 10110111</code><br><br>(d) Encontra um padrão de erros que o checksum não deteta, e mostra a verificação.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p>Palavras de 16 bits, por ordem: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_1</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0100101001101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_2</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101101100101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_3</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000010000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_4</annotation></semantics></math> <code>0000000000000000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_5</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1010001010101010</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_6</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000000111110101</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_7</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1101000111101000</code>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_8</annotation></semantics></math> <code>1000101010110111</code>.</p>\n<p>Na <strong>mesma coluna</strong> de duas palavras, um 0 passa a 1 numa e um 1 passa a 0 na outra. Por exemplo, o último bit de <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_5</annotation></semantics></math> (0 → 1: <code>1010001010101011</code>, mais 1) e o último bit de <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w_8</annotation></semantics></math> (1 → 0: <code>1000101010110110</code>, menos 1). A soma não muda: o receptor obtém outra vez <code>1111111111111111</code> e <strong>não deteta</strong> o erro. (Trocar duas palavras de ordem também passa despercebido.)</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> um 0→1 e um 1→0 na mesma coluna.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#udp-e-o-checksum\" target=\"_blank\">📖 UDP e o checksum</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F61a", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 1 — Stop-and-wait.</b> O Fábio fez um protocolo stop-and-wait para uma rede onde se perdem pacotes (sem erros de bit). O emissor: \"espera dados\" → envia e passa a \"espera confirmação\"; timeout → reenvia; confirmação → volta a \"espera dados\".<br><br>(a) Explica porque é que as confirmações também precisam de número de sequência (desenha o cenário).", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p>Por causa dos <strong><em>timeouts</em> prematuros</strong> (ou de ACKs que só se atrasam). Sem números:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>o emissor envia o pacote P1 e o ACK atrasa-se;</li>\n<li>dá <em>timeout</em> e retransmite P1;</li>\n<li>chega o 1.º ACK (de P1): o emissor envia P2;</li>\n<li>P2 perde-se, mas chega o 2.º ACK, que é da <strong>retransmissão</strong> de P1;</li>\n<li>sem número, o emissor toma-o como confirmação de <strong>P2</strong> e avança: P2 perdeu-se e ninguém deu por isso.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Com o número (1 bit chega, 0/1), o 2.º ACK diz “ACK de P1” e o emissor, que espera o ACK de P2, ignora-o. (Os pacotes também precisam de número, para o receptor descartar o P1 duplicado.)</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> timeout prematuro: o ACK atrasado confirma o pacote errado.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#princípios-da-transferência-fiável\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Princípios da transferência\nfiável</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F61b", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 1 — Stop-and-wait.</b> O Fábio fez um protocolo stop-and-wait para uma rede onde se perdem pacotes (sem erros de bit). O emissor: \"espera dados\" → envia e passa a \"espera confirmação\"; timeout → reenvia; confirmação → volta a \"espera dados\".<br><br>(b) O protocolo é adequado para 10 Mbps, propagação de 20 ms e pacotes de 1500 bytes? Calcula a utilização.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><ol type=\"1\">\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1500</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>/</mi><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>000</mn><mi>/</mi><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/R = 1500\\times8/10^7 = 12\\,000/10^7 = 1{,}2\\times10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> s <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 1{,}2</annotation></semantics></math> ms.</li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">RTT = 2\\times20 = 40</annotation></semantics></math> ms.</li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U = \\dfrac{L/R}{RTT + L/R} = \\dfrac{1{,}2}{41{,}2} \\approx 0{,}029</annotation></semantics></math>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Não é adequado</strong>: a ligação só está ocupada cerca de 3% do tempo (débito <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>029</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\approx 0{,}029\\times10</annotation></semantics></math> Mbps <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>290</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\approx 290</annotation></semantics></math> kbps). Para transmissão contínua seriam precisos <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>41</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>34</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">41{,}2/1{,}2 \\approx 34{,}3</annotation></semantics></math>, ou seja, <strong>35 pacotes em trânsito</strong> (<em>pipelining</em>). Solução oficial: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>029</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">U \\approx 0{,}029</annotation></semantics></math>, “não é adequado”.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> U = (L/R)/(RTT + L/R).<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#stop-and-wait-e-a-sua-utilização\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Stop-and-wait e a sua\nutilização</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F62b", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 2 — Repetições seletivas.</b> Selective Repeat em que, em cada instante, o emissor só pode enviar uma mensagem; uma mensagem chega no instante seguinte, o receptor responde logo, e retransmite-se ao fim de 3 instantes sem confirmação.<br><br>(b) Faz o esquema (instante a instante) para 5 blocos (0 a 4), janela 3 e timeout 3, perdendo-se o bloco 3 e a confirmação do bloco 2. Faz no papel e compara.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p>Regras: em cada instante o emissor envia no máximo uma mensagem; uma mensagem enviada no instante <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t</annotation></semantics></math> chega em <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t+1</annotation></semantics></math> e o receptor responde logo, por isso o ACK chega ao emissor em <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t+2</annotation></semantics></math>; sem ACK, reenvia em <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">t+3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<table style=\"width:100%;\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 30%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 23%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 23%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 23%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: center;\">instante</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">emissor</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">mensagem</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">receptor</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">janela [0,2]; envia B(0)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(0) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">2</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">envia B(1)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(1) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(0), entrega-o; envia A(0); janela [1,3]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">3</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe A(0): janela [1,3]; envia B(2)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(2) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(1), entrega-o; envia A(1); janela [2,4]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">4</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe A(1): janela [2,4]; envia B(3)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(3) ✕ perdido</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(2), entrega-o; envia A(2) ✕ perdido; janela [3,5]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">5</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">envia B(4)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(4) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">(nada chega)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">6</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"><em>timeout</em> de B(2) (enviado em 3): reenvia B(2)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(2) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(4): fora de ordem → <em>buffer</em>; envia A(4)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">7</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe A(4): marca o 4; <em>timeout</em> de B(3) (enviado em 4): reenvia B(3)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">B(3) →</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(2): já entregue (em [0,2]), reenvia A(2)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">8</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe A(2): janela [3,5]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe B(3): entrega 3 e 4; envia A(3); janela [5,7]</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">9</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">recebe A(3): tudo confirmado, janela [5,7]</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>O B(4) <strong>não</strong> é retransmitido: o A(4) chega no instante 7, antes do seu <em>timeout</em> (5 + 3 = 8). No instante 7 o receptor tem de voltar a confirmar o B(2), que já tinha entregue: sem esse ACK, o emissor ficava a retransmitir B(2) para sempre. A solução oficial é uma figura (não transcrita no Moodle); confere com ela os instantes.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> SR: buffer fora de ordem, re-ACK de pacotes antigos, só se reenvia o que expira.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#pipelining-go-back-n-e-selective-repeat\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Pipelining:\nGo-Back-N e Selective Repeat</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F64a", "<b>Ficha 6, Ex. 4 — Size matters?</b> Fibra de 5000 km a 2 Gbps (v ≈ 2×10<sup>8</sup> m/s), Selective Repeat com blocos de 1000 B. (a) Quantos blocos tem de ter a janela para fluxo contínuo? Quantos bits de número de sequência?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><ol type=\"1\">\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m</mtext></mrow><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mrow><mspace width=\"0.333em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\"> m/s</mtext></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>025</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">d_{prop} = 5\\times10^6\\text{ m} / 2\\times10^8\\text{ m/s} = 0{,}025</annotation></semantics></math> s; <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">RTT = 0{,}05</annotation></semantics></math> s.</li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mi>−</mi><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L/R = 1000\\times8 / 2\\times10^9 = 4\\times10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> s.</li>\n<li>Fluxo contínuo quando o 1.º ACK chega mesmo antes de a janela acabar: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">N\\cdot L/R \\ge RTT + L/R</annotation></semantics></math>, logo $N  = 12,500 + 1 = $ <strong>12 501 blocos</strong>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Números de sequência: no SR a gama tem de ter <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>002</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2N = 25\\,002</annotation></semantics></math> números; <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>14</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>384</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>25</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>002</mn><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2^{14} = 16\\,384 &lt; 25\\,002 \\le 2^{15} = 32\\,768</annotation></semantics></math>, por isso <strong>15 bits</strong>. Solução oficial: 12 501 blocos.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> janela = (RTT + L/R)/(L/R); SR precisa de gama ≥ 2N.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#pipelining-go-back-n-e-selective-repeat\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Pipelining:\nGo-Back-N e Selective Repeat</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F73d", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 3 — Timeout.</b> Estimação do RTT com α = 0,1 e β = 0,2. Os RTT medidos foram 54, 63, 55, 57, 68, 56, 55 e 58 ms. O EstimatedRTT inicial é o 1.º RTT e o DevRTT inicial metade dele. Que timeout se usa para o pacote seguinte? Faz a tabela.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha = 0{,}1</annotation></semantics></math>; SampleRTT(1) é a amostra mais recente.</p>\n<p>Valores iniciais: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E = 54</annotation></semantics></math>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D = 54/2 = 27</annotation></semantics></math>. Para cada amostra <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math>, pela ordem da receita: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>←</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>D</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D \\leftarrow 0{,}8D + 0{,}2|S - E|</annotation></semantics></math> (com o <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math> antigo) e depois <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>←</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E \\leftarrow 0{,}9E + 0{,}1S</annotation></semantics></math>. A 1.ª amostra (54) também entra.</p>\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 20%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\lvert S-E\\rvert</annotation></semantics></math></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">D</annotation></semantics></math> novo</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math> novo</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E + 4D</annotation></semantics></math></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">54</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">0{,}8\\cdot27 = 21{,}6</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">54</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">140,4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">63</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">9</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>08</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">17{,}28 + 1{,}8 = 19{,}08</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">48{,}6 + 6{,}3 = 54{,}9</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">131,22</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">55</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0,1</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>264</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>284</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15{,}264 + 0{,}02 = 15{,}284</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>49</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>41</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>54</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>91</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">49{,}41 + 5{,}5 = 54{,}91</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">116,05</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">57</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">2,09</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>227</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>418</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>645</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">12{,}227 + 0{,}418 = 12{,}645</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>49</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>419</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>119</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">49{,}419 + 5{,}7 = 55{,}119</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">105,70</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">68</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">12,881</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>116</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>576</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>692</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10{,}116 + 2{,}576 = 12{,}692</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>49</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>607</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>407</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">49{,}607 + 6{,}8 = 56{,}407</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">107,18</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">56</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">0,407</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>154</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>081</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>235</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">10{,}154 + 0{,}081 = 10{,}235</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>766</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>366</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">50{,}766 + 5{,}6 = 56{,}366</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">97,31</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">55</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,366</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>188</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>462</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">8{,}188 + 0{,}273 = 8{,}462</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>730</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>230</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">50{,}730 + 5{,}5 = 56{,}230</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">90,08</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">58</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\">1,770</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>769</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>354</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>123</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">6{,}769 + 0{,}354 = 7{,}123</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>607</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>407</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">50{,}607 + 5{,}8 = 56{,}407</annotation></semantics></math></td>\n<td style=\"text-align: right;\"><strong>84,90</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Timeout ≈ 84,9 ms</strong> (igual à solução oficial). Nota: só se chega aos 84,9 com estas duas escolhas (a 1.ª amostra também entra, e o DevRTT usa o <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math> antigo). Sem a 1.ª amostra daria 89,4 ms; com o <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math> novo, 83,9 ms; com os valores típicos <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>125</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha = 0{,}125</annotation></semantics></math>, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\beta = 0{,}25</annotation></semantics></math>, 78,4 ms.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> D com o E antigo; a 1.ª amostra também entra; timeout = E + 4D.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#estimar-o-rtt-e-escolher-o-timeout\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Estimar o RTT e escolher o\ntimeout</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F73a", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 3 — Timeout.</b> Estimação do RTT com α = 0,1 e β = 0,2. SampleRTT(1) é a mais recente. (a) Com 4 amostras, SampleRTT(4) a SampleRTT(1), escreve o EstimatedRTT em função delas.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\alpha = 0{,}1</annotation></semantics></math>; SampleRTT(1) é a amostra mais recente.</p>\n<p>O valor inicial é a 1.ª amostra, SampleRTT(4). Aplicando a fórmula três vezes:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>depois de S(3): <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E = (1-\\alpha)S(4) + \\alpha S(3)</annotation></semantics></math>;</li>\n<li>depois de S(2): <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E = (1-\\alpha)^2 S(4) + \\alpha(1-\\alpha) S(3) + \\alpha S(2)</annotation></semantics></math>;</li>\n<li>depois de S(1): <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E = \\alpha S(1) + \\alpha(1-\\alpha) S(2) + \\alpha(1-\\alpha)^2 S(3) + (1-\\alpha)^3 S(4)</annotation></semantics></math> <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>09</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>081</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>729</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 0{,}1\\,S(1) + 0{,}09\\,S(2) + 0{,}081\\,S(3) + 0{,}729\\,S(4).</annotation></semantics></math></li>\n</ol>\n<p>(Os pesos somam 1. A mais antiga pesa tanto porque também é o valor inicial.)</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> aplica a fórmula 3 vezes a partir de S(4).<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#estimar-o-rtt-e-escolher-o-timeout\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Estimar o RTT e escolher o\ntimeout</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F74", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 4 — Controlo de congestionamento.</b> A figura é a janela de um TCP Reno (MSS) por ronda (RTT).<br><img src=\"assets/guia-redes/reno_f7.png\" alt=\"janela do TCP Reno por ronda\" style=\"max-width:100%\"><br>(h) Em que ronda é transmitido o 70.º segmento? (Confirma também: limiar inicial, tipo de perda nas rondas 16 e 22, e limiar nas rondas 18 e 24.)", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>(c)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p><strong>Triplo ACK duplicado</strong>: a janela passa de 42 para <strong>21</strong>, metade (e continua a crescer linearmente). Um <em>timeout</em> levava-a a 1.</p>\n<p><strong>(d)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p><strong><em>Timeout</em></strong>: a janela passa de 26 para <strong>1</strong> MSS e volta ao <em>slow start</em>.</p>\n<p><strong>(e)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p><strong>32 MSS</strong>: é onde o crescimento passa de exponencial (até 32, na ronda 6) a linear (33 na ronda 7).</p>\n<p><strong>(f)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p>Na perda do fim da ronda 16 a janela era 42: limiar $= 42/2 = $ <strong>21 MSS</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>(g)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p>Na perda do fim da ronda 22 a janela era 26: limiar $= 26/2 = $ <strong>13 MSS</strong>. (A ronda 26, com 8, ainda está abaixo dele, em <em>slow start</em>.)</p>\n<p><strong>(h)</strong> Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p>Segmentos acumulados: ronda 1: 1; 2: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1+2 = 3</annotation></semantics></math>; 3: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">3+4 = 7</annotation></semantics></math>; 4: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">7+8 =\n15</annotation></semantics></math>; 5: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">15+16 = 31</annotation></semantics></math>; 6: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>31</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">31+32 = 63</annotation></semantics></math>; 7: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>63</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">63+33 = 96</annotation></semantics></math>. Os segmentos 64 a 96 saem na ronda 7, por isso o 70.º sai na <strong>ronda 7</strong>.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> soma as janelas ronda a ronda; metade = 3 ACKs dup., 1 = timeout.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#controlo-de-congestionamento-no-tcp\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Controlo de\ncongestionamento no TCP</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F74i", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 4 — Controlo de congestionamento.</b> A figura é a janela de um TCP Reno (MSS) por ronda (RTT).<br><img src=\"assets/guia-redes/reno_f7.png\" alt=\"janela do TCP Reno por ronda\" style=\"max-width:100%\"><br>(i) Se depois da ronda 26 houver uma perda por triplo ACK duplicado, quais ficam a ser a janela e o limiar?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p>Leitura do gráfico, ronda a ronda: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32 (rondas 1–6); 33 a 42 (rondas 7–16); 21 a 26 (17–22); 1, 2, 4, 8 (23–26).</p>\n<p>Na ronda 26 a janela é 8: limiar <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 8/2 = 4</annotation></semantics></math> e CongWin <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= 4</annotation></semantics></math> (Reno: CongWin = limiar). <strong>Ambos 4 MSS.</strong></p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> Reno, 3 ACKs dup.: limiar = janela = W/2.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#controlo-de-congestionamento-no-tcp\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Controlo de\ncongestionamento no TCP</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-C32b", "<b>Treino — retransmissão rápida.</b> A envia a B segmentos de 500, 300 e 200 bytes a partir do byte 1000; o 1500 perde-se, o 1800 chega. A envia depois mais três segmentos de 100 bytes, que chegam todos. B guarda os segmentos fora de ordem e confirma cada um logo.<br><br>(a) Que números de sequência e que ACKs têm os três segmentos novos? (b) Quando é que A retransmite o 1500? (c) Que ACK envia B quando o 1500 chega?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>(a)</strong> Situação: o 1000 (500 B) chegou (<code>ACK=1500</code>), o 1500 (300 B) perdeu-se, e o 1800 (200 B) chegou fora de ordem (<code>ACK=1500</code>, <strong>1.º duplicado</strong>).</p>\n<p>Continuam a partir do último byte enviado (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>1800</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">1800 + 200 = 2000</annotation></semantics></math>): sequências <strong>2000</strong>, <strong>2100</strong> e <strong>2200</strong> (100 bytes cada). Todos chegam fora de ordem (o buraco 1500–1799 continua), por isso cada um gera <code>ACK=1500</code> (2.º, 3.º e 4.º duplicados).</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> Situação: o 1000 (500 B) chegou (<code>ACK=1500</code>), o 1500 (300 B) perdeu-se, e o 1800 (200 B) chegou fora de ordem (<code>ACK=1500</code>, <strong>1.º duplicado</strong>).</p>\n<p>Contando os duplicados de 1500: o do 1800 é o 1.º, o do 2000 o 2.º e o do 2100 o <strong>3.º</strong>. Quando A recebe o ACK duplicado gerado pelo segmento <strong>2100</strong>, retransmite logo o 1500, sem esperar pelo <em>timeout</em>. (O 4.º duplicado, do 2200, já não volta a provocar retransmissão.)</p>\n<p><strong>(c)</strong> Situação: o 1000 (500 B) chegou (<code>ACK=1500</code>), o 1500 (300 B) perdeu-se, e o 1800 (200 B) chegou fora de ordem (<code>ACK=1500</code>, <strong>1.º duplicado</strong>).</p>\n<p>B passa a ter os bytes 1000 a 2299 seguidos (o 1500 tapa o buraco; o 1800, 2000, 2100 e 2200 estavam no <em>buffer</em>): envia <strong><code>ACK=2300</code></strong>, que confirma tudo de uma vez.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> conta os ACKs duplicados: o 3.º duplicado dispara a retransmissão.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#tcp-transferência-fiável-e-retransmissão-rápida\" target=\"_blank\">📖 TCP:\ntransferência fiável e retransmissão rápida</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F81a", "<b>Ficha 8, Ex. 1 — De janelas e perdas.</b> TCP Reno em congestion avoidance: a janela (em MSS) varia entre W/2 e W, quando uma perda a reduz a metade.<br><br>(a) Mostra que a taxa de perdas é ≈ 8/(3W²). (b) Deduz que o débito é ≈ 1,22·MSS/(RTT·√L).", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>(a)</strong> <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L</annotation></semantics></math> = pacotes perdidos / pacotes enviados. Num ciclo (de uma perda à seguinte) perde-se <strong>1</strong> pacote. A janela começa em <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W/2</annotation></semantics></math> e sobe 1 por RTT até <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>: são as janelas <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>…</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W/2,\\ W/2+1,\\ \\ldots,\\ W</annotation></semantics></math> (<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W/2 + 1</annotation></semantics></math> rondas). Pacotes enviados num ciclo: <math display=\"block\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\sum_{n=0}^{W/2}\\left(\\frac W2 + n\\right)\n= \\frac W2\\left(\\frac W2 + 1\\right) + \\frac{\\frac W2\\left(\\frac W2+1\\right)}{2}\n= \\frac{W^2}{4} + \\frac W2 + \\frac{W^2}{8} + \\frac W4\n= \\frac38 W^2 + \\frac34 W.</annotation></semantics></math> Logo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L = \\dfrac{1}{\\frac38W^2 + \\frac34W}</annotation></semantics></math>. Para <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math> grande, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≫</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac38W^2 \\gg \\frac34W</annotation></semantics></math>, e <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">L \\approx \\dfrac{8}{3W^2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> 1. De (a): <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W^2 \\approx \\dfrac{8}{3L}</annotation></semantics></math>, logo <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>≈</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W \\approx \\sqrt{\\dfrac{8}{3L}}</annotation></semantics></math>. 2. A janela varia linearmente entre <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mi>/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W/2</annotation></semantics></math> e <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">W</annotation></semantics></math>: em média <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac34W</annotation></semantics></math> segmentos por RTT, isto é, débito <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">MSS</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= \\dfrac34\\cdot\\dfrac{W\\cdot\\text{MSS}}{RTT}</annotation></semantics></math>. 3. Substituindo: débito <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">MSS</mtext><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">= \\dfrac34\\sqrt{\\dfrac83}\\cdot\\dfrac{\\text{MSS}}{RTT\\sqrt L}</annotation></semantics></math>, e <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>633</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\dfrac34\\sqrt{\\dfrac83} = 0{,}75\\times1{,}633 \\approx 1{,}22</annotation></semantics></math>. Logo débito <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">MSS</mtext></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>⋅</mo><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\approx \\dfrac{1{,}22\\cdot\\text{MSS}}{RTT\\cdot\\sqrt L}</annotation></semantics></math> bytes/s.</p>\n<p>(Igual à resolução oficial, <code>Praticas/Semana_8/F8ex1.pdf</code>.)</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> segmentos num ciclo = Σ(W/2 + n), n = 0..W/2; 1 perda por ciclo.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#controlo-de-congestionamento-no-tcp\" target=\"_blank\">📖 Controlo de\ncongestionamento no TCP</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F72a", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 2 — Hello Goodbye.</b> (a) Explica o three-way handshake: para que serve e como se processa. (b) Como se terminam as conexões TCP?", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><p><strong>(a)</strong> Serve para <strong>inicializar as variáveis da conexão</strong> nos dois lados antes dos dados: os <strong>números de sequência iniciais</strong> de cada sentido e os <em>buffers</em>/janela do receptor. Processa-se em três segmentos:</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li><strong>SYN</strong> (cliente → servidor): sem dados, com o número de sequência inicial do cliente, <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x</annotation></semantics></math>;</li>\n<li><strong>SYN+ACK</strong> (servidor → cliente): o servidor reserva os <em>buffers</em>, envia o seu número inicial <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">y</annotation></semantics></math> e confirma o do cliente (<code>ACK = x+1</code>);</li>\n<li><strong>ACK</strong> (cliente → servidor): <code>ACK = y+1</code>; já pode levar dados.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>São precisos três porque cada lado tem de saber que o outro recebeu o seu número inicial: o 2.º segmento confirma o do cliente, o 3.º o do servidor.</p>\n<p><strong>(b)</strong> Cada sentido fecha em separado (a conexão é <em>full duplex</em>):</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>quem fecha primeiro (p. ex. o cliente, <code>close()</code>) envia <strong>FIN</strong>;</li>\n<li>o outro responde <strong>ACK</strong> (pode ainda enviar dados) e, quando a aplicação dele também fechar, envia o seu <strong>FIN</strong>;</li>\n<li>o primeiro responde <strong>ACK</strong> e fica em <strong>TIME_WAIT</strong> (2 vezes o tempo de vida de um segmento), para voltar a responder com ACK se o FIN se repetir (o último ACK pode perder-se);</li>\n<li>ao receber esse ACK, o outro lado fecha; o primeiro fecha quando acaba o TIME_WAIT.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Solução oficial: SYN, SYN+ACK e ACK; FIN e ACK + FIN e ACK.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> SYN(x) → SYN+ACK(y, x+1) → ACK(y+1); fecho FIN/ACK em cada sentido.<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#tcp-controlo-de-fluxo-e-gestão-de-conexões\" target=\"_blank\">📖 TCP: controlo de\nfluxo e gestão de conexões</a>"],
  ["Parte II · Transporte", "D-F71", "<b>Ficha 7, Ex. 1 — Controla o quê?</b> Explica as diferenças entre o controlo de fluxo e o controlo de congestionamento: objetivos e entidade ativa de cada um.", null, -1, "<div class=\"sol-title\">Resolução</div><div class=\"sol-aberta\"><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 33%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\"></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">controlo de fluxo</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">controlo de congestionamento</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">objetivo</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">o emissor não envia mais depressa do que o <strong>receptor</strong> consegue processar (não extravasar o <em>buffer</em> dele)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">o emissor não envia mais depressa do que a <strong>rede</strong> consegue levar até ao receptor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">entidade ativa</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">o <strong>receptor</strong>, que anuncia a RcvWindow (espaço livre no <em>buffer</em>)</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">o <strong>emissor</strong>, que infere o congestionamento pelas perdas (3 ACKs dup. ou <em>timeout</em>) e reduz a CongWin</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>As duas janelas são limites superiores à janela de <em>pipelining</em>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">LastByteSent</mtext><mo>−</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">LastByteAcked</mtext><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">min</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"prefix\">(</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">CongWin</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">RcvWindow</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\" form=\"postfix\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\text{LastByteSent} - \\text{LastByteAcked} \\le \\min(\\text{CongWin}, \\text{RcvWindow})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n</div>", "<b>Para lembrar:</b> fluxo = receptor (RcvWindow); congestionamento = emissor (CongWin).<br>Se a resolução não chegou, lê a teoria: <a class=\"teoria\" href=\"guia_redes_teste1.html#tcp-controlo-de-fluxo-e-gestão-de-conexões\" target=\"_blank\">📖 TCP: controlo de\nfluxo e gestão de conexões</a>"],
];
